      "program_name": "Novato Affordable Housing Fund (inclusionary in-lieu fee fund) gap financing and development fee waivers for affordable projects",
      "administering_agency": "City of Novato Community Development Department, 922 Machin Avenue, Novato, (415) 899-8989",
      "funding_type": "loan",
      "typical_award_size": "No published guidelines or NOFA located. The City's housing page (not openable this pass) states that developers of affordable housing may request City gap financing to complete a project's funding, and Council actions have used the Affordable Housing Fund for loans and fee relief: Homeward Bound and Habitat for Humanity loans historically; $1,000,000 allocated in 2023 and about $1,000,000 more in reductions and waivers of City permitting fees approved March 2025 for Habitat's 80-unit Redwood Boulevard project (construction expected 2026). Fund balance was about $1,200,000 in 2019; current balance unknown.",
      "per_unit_cap": null,
      "affordability_requirement": "Set per agreement; Division 19.24 requires in-lieu funds be spent on very low, low and moderate income housing. Habitat project is ownership housing for low and moderate income buyers.",
