        "acquisition-rehab",
        "preservation",
        "supportive housing"
      ],
      "application_cycle": "rolling",
      "next_deadline": "unknown, verify with agency. No NOFA found; requests go to Council through the Community Development Department.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "Treat as a small, negotiated gap source of roughly $1,000,000 per project at most, used mainly to unlock Marin County Affordable Housing Fund loans (County guidelines require a city contribution) and County PLHA; CDBG and HOME for Novato flow through the Marin Urban County planning area. Fee waivers and City loans are public funds for Labor Code 1720 purposes. No commercial linkage fee exists in the Novato Zoning Ordinance as mirrored. Figures for the Habitat project and gap financing language come from search result snippets of novato.gov pages and a Marin County news release that could not be opened; the source_url is the code mirror establishing the fund (19.24.040). novato.gov and novato.org returned 403 to every request this pass (HTML pages, showpublisheddocument PDFs and the news module); Novato has no Legistar API client and no Granicus or IQM2 host was found, so City pages, the 2023-2031 Housing Element, the 2025 Annual Progress Report and Council staff reports could not be opened. The Zoning Ordinance was read on the Zoneomics mirror and HCD's April 12, 2023 review letter was opened on hcd.ca.gov. marincounty.gov remained Cloudflare-blocked this pass; County programs are referenced from the Marin County records in this database.",
